WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:41.730
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
01:42.000 --> 01:44.840
You had me gathering market data on digital collectibles for so long.

3
01:44.920 --> 01:46.920
What are you planning to do to Wen Ruosen?

4
01:54.040 --> 01:55.040
Take a look at this.

5
01:57.440 --> 01:59.040
WEN RUOSEN, FOUNDER OF YUANZHOU GALLERY

6
01:59.120 --> 02:00.320
I already know all this.

7
02:01.240 --> 02:02.480
He used to be your mentor,

8
02:02.560 --> 02:04.240
and you worked under him for quite a while before you left the firm.

9
02:06.480 --> 02:07.800
Do you know why I left Boen?

10
02:09.880 --> 02:10.720
Back then,

11
02:11.320 --> 02:12.880
Wen Ruosen screwed me over badly.

12
02:15.480 --> 02:17.840
Back then, he was only a junior partner,

13
02:18.880 --> 02:20.040
and I was a young consultant

14
02:20.120 --> 02:21.360
who looked up to him wholeheartedly like an elder brother.

15
02:22.000 --> 02:24.280
Boen landed the transformation project for Jingshang Department Store.

16
02:24.360 --> 02:26.480
He led the team and drafted a plan to turn Jingshang Department Store

17
02:26.560 --> 02:27.920
into a chain brand.

18
02:28.560 --> 02:30.040
But halfway through the project,

19
02:30.120 --> 02:32.880
he realized the plan was ill-suited for local conditions

20
02:32.960 --> 02:34.880
and would definitely lead to massive losses down the line.

21
02:35.600 --> 02:37.720
So he suddenly promoted me to PM.

22
02:39.680 --> 02:41.520
At that time, I thought I was so lucky,

23
02:42.160 --> 02:44.760
like a thoroughbred steed spotted by a discerning talent.

24
02:45.280 --> 02:47.560
Little did I know, he promoted me just…

25
02:47.640 --> 02:50.080
To save his own skin and to make you take the fall?

26
02:50.160 --> 02:51.360
Exactly.

27
02:52.000 --> 02:53.600
Less than two months after the handover,

28
02:53.680 --> 02:55.080
Jingshang Department Store hit disaster.

29
02:55.160 --> 02:56.280
It was a treasured, time-honored enterprise

30
02:56.360 --> 02:57.680
with 60 years of history.

31
02:57.760 --> 02:58.960
Boen's reputation was ruined overnight.

32
02:59.040 --> 03:01.880
Luckily, the internet wasn't as widespread back then.

33
03:01.960 --> 03:03.480
The headquarters spent an eight-figure PR budget

34
03:03.560 --> 03:05.280
to contain the scandal.

35
03:06.160 --> 03:07.880
As the project manager,

36
03:08.480 --> 03:09.480
I had to resign.

37
03:09.560 --> 03:11.080
But what about Wen Ruosen?

38
03:11.160 --> 03:13.120
Didn't he bear any responsibility?

39
03:15.000 --> 03:19.840
He left hundreds of Jingshang employees jobless and destitute.

40
03:20.640 --> 03:22.640
But I couldn't stand him tricking me into taking the fall,

41
03:23.160 --> 03:24.560
ruining all those people's lives,

42
03:24.640 --> 03:26.600
and walking away scot-free.

43
03:26.680 --> 03:30.880
Later, he even wrote me a glowing recommendation letter.

44
03:30.960 --> 03:33.760
For a time, I was deeply grateful to him.

45
03:34.640 --> 03:35.480
Later,

46
03:35.560 --> 03:38.200
after I applied to every consulting firm in Beijing

47
03:39.040 --> 03:40.320
and got rejected by all of them,

48
03:42.320 --> 03:43.600
it suddenly dawned on me.

49
03:43.680 --> 03:45.520
So you were…

50
03:46.240 --> 03:49.560
You're trying to say I was naive and foolish.

51
03:52.080 --> 03:53.600
I've always wondered

52
03:53.680 --> 03:55.640
what you were like when you were naive and foolish.

53
04:01.800 --> 04:03.560
Go ahead, take a look.

54
04:14.640 --> 04:15.760
So you moved to Shenzhen afterwards?

55
04:19.680 --> 04:22.360
Back then, I lost nearly everything.

56
04:23.360 --> 04:25.640
Yet I refused to give up so easily.

57
04:25.720 --> 04:28.160
Up north, most firms were foreign-owned,

58
04:28.240 --> 04:30.200
so I decided to try my luck in the Pearl River Delta.

59
04:31.000 --> 04:33.280
Plenty of enterprises were growing wildly there,

60
04:33.360 --> 04:36.320
alongside many homegrown consulting firms rising rapidly.

61
04:36.400 --> 04:37.560
I revised my resume,

62
04:37.640 --> 04:40.120
erased my work experience at Boen,

63
04:40.200 --> 04:42.680
and joined a mid-sized company with Hong Kong capital backing.

64
04:42.760 --> 04:43.600
MILK TEA, BEEF TRIPE, DESSERT HOUSE TEAROOM, STREET FOOD

65
04:43.680 --> 04:44.960
I kept grinding away

66
04:45.040 --> 04:46.960
and gradually built up a bit of a reputation.

67
04:47.040 --> 04:48.080
That's when I met Du.

68
04:48.160 --> 04:50.000
He recruited me to start a venture together.

69
04:50.080 --> 04:52.320
Later I found out Du had also been screwed over

70
04:52.400 --> 04:54.040
by Wen Ruosen, just like me.

71
04:54.120 --> 04:58.000
What's more, his father was a long-time employee at Jingshang.

72
04:58.080 --> 05:00.600
Wen Ruosen cost all of them their jobs.

73
05:01.120 --> 05:03.120
Victims deserve compensation.

74
05:03.200 --> 05:05.000
Wen Ruosen has to pay the price, just like I did.

75
05:05.800 --> 05:07.080
It took me two years

76
05:07.160 --> 05:09.280
to finally land a project for a major American brand

77
05:09.360 --> 05:10.200
launching in China.

78
05:11.080 --> 05:12.680
I even won the Constantine Award.

79
05:13.280 --> 05:14.600
The Constantine Award?

80
05:14.680 --> 05:16.160
The highest honor from the International Consulting Alliance?

81
05:16.240 --> 05:17.520
It was only silver,

82
05:17.600 --> 05:20.200
but I finally had the money to compensate the victims from Jingshang.

83
05:20.280 --> 05:22.440
I also earned my way back into the top consulting circle.

84
05:23.400 --> 05:26.160
After that, I joined P&J to gain hands-on operational experience.

85
05:27.360 --> 05:29.480
Then I moved to Hezong.

86
05:29.560 --> 05:31.760
That was when you interviewed me?

87
05:33.040 --> 05:35.560
That was our first meeting.

88
05:37.040 --> 05:40.920
So what was I like in your eyes back then?

89
05:41.000 --> 05:44.640
Some kid who knew nothing yet tried hard to pretend to be an elite?

90
05:46.000 --> 05:47.280
Back then, you were

91
05:47.360 --> 05:49.480
a pretty proud, promising young woman.

92
05:49.560 --> 05:50.880
You shone bright.

93
05:54.440 --> 05:56.040
I was just thinking.

94
05:56.120 --> 05:57.760
By having me do all this work,

95
05:57.840 --> 05:58.920
are you trying to set a trap for him?

96
06:00.600 --> 06:01.640
Yes.

97
06:01.720 --> 06:03.480
But doesn't he have any defenses at all?

98
06:03.560 --> 06:05.560
He screwed you over before. He must know what he did.

99
06:05.640 --> 06:07.200
Over all these years,

100
06:07.280 --> 06:08.480
he's hurt so many people.

101
06:08.560 --> 06:09.480
He can't even keep count.

102
06:09.560 --> 06:11.720
And after so many years,

103
06:11.800 --> 06:13.760
he's long rationalized all the terrible things he did.

104
06:13.840 --> 06:16.080
By now, he probably thinks what he did back then

105
06:16.160 --> 06:17.360
was no big deal at all.

106
06:18.040 --> 06:21.240
Anyway, I send him text messages on every holiday.

107
06:21.320 --> 06:23.360
And when we meet, I'm always grateful to him.

108
06:24.240 --> 06:27.080
I think he's got no defenses at all.

109
06:28.640 --> 06:30.800
You're such a crafty old fox.

110
06:34.760 --> 06:35.800
Alright.

111
06:36.360 --> 06:38.600
From now on, I'll call you Officer Rabbit.

112
06:43.600 --> 06:46.280
Officer Rabbit will definitely help you take Wen Ruosen down.

113
06:46.800 --> 06:48.480
Just tell me what exactly I need to do.

114
06:50.480 --> 06:51.400
You've already done it.

115
06:58.960 --> 07:00.000
Look at this.

116
07:03.200 --> 07:05.640
YE XINZHI: WHEN ARE YOU GOING TO GIVE ME MY PITCHFORK?

117
07:10.080 --> 07:11.280
MESSAGE

118
07:11.360 --> 07:12.240
WEN RUOSEN

119
07:12.320 --> 07:13.240
WEN RUOSEN: SAW YOUR POSTS. YOU AND MR. DENG FROM MORSE KNOW EACH OTHER?

120
07:13.320 --> 07:14.320
YE: YEAH, WE'VE KNOWN FOR SIX, SEVEN YEARS

121
07:14.400 --> 07:15.360
WEN: YOU TWO PRETTY CLOSE? HE EVEN ASKED YOU TO PLAY SPORTS

122
07:15.440 --> 07:16.400
YE: WE GET ON OKAY, I SUPPOSE FIRST MET AT THEIR COMPANY ANNUAL DINNER

123
07:16.480 --> 07:17.400
YE: WE'VE WORKED ON A FEW PROJECTS

124
07:17.480 --> 07:18.480
WEN: GOOD FOR YOU ANY COLLABORATION RECENTLY?

125
07:18.560 --> 07:19.440
WEN: ANY IDEA HOW INTERESTED THEY ARE IN THE METAVERSE NEW ECONOMY?

126
07:19.520 --> 07:20.400
YE: FAIRLY INTERESTED. THEY BACKED XINHONG IN Q1 FOR BLOCKCHAIN SMART CONTRACTS

127
07:21.040 --> 07:22.640
You're setting a trap.

128
07:22.720 --> 07:25.080
Don't say anything. Let me guess.

129
07:27.640 --> 07:29.120
Wen Ruosen's Yuanzhou Digital Collectibles

130
07:29.200 --> 07:32.320
is essentially a reseller for high-priced digital collectibles.

131
07:32.400 --> 07:33.960
Since the collections he represents

132
07:34.040 --> 07:35.680
are works by renowned artists, they carry sky-high valuations.

133
07:35.760 --> 07:36.880
But the business has never turned a profit.

134
07:36.960 --> 07:38.440
Wen Ruosen is drowning in debt.

135
07:38.520 --> 07:40.320
If he wants to keep maintaining those high valuations,

136
07:40.400 --> 07:42.840
he needs to create new business scenarios.

137
07:43.440 --> 07:45.920
Benyuan Digital Collectibles, which we ran into at the forum last time,

138
07:46.000 --> 07:47.480
is Hong Kong's largest digital collectibles platform.

139
07:47.560 --> 07:50.360
That's why Wen Ruosen kept trying to persuade them to take a stake.

140
07:50.440 --> 07:53.160
But their cooperation has been going nowhere.

141
07:53.680 --> 07:55.200
Did you do something behind the scenes?

142
07:55.280 --> 07:58.160
I had you gather plenty of information on Benyuan Digital Collectibles,

143
07:58.240 --> 08:00.320
asked Du to prepare several rounds of free financial analysis

144
08:00.400 --> 08:01.520
for Yong'an Trust,

145
08:01.600 --> 08:03.680
the major investor of Benyuan, and Yong'an pulled out.

146
08:03.760 --> 08:06.240
So Wen Ruosen has to look for other funding sources.

147
08:07.000 --> 08:09.600
In fact, he approached Morse before,

148
08:09.680 --> 08:10.920
but got nothing out of it.

149
08:11.000 --> 08:13.520
He found that I've recently been working closely with Morse

150
08:13.600 --> 08:14.640
on the Tianhe Air project,

151
08:14.720 --> 08:15.720
so he came to me.

152
08:16.320 --> 08:18.200
He wants you to broker financing with Morse.

153
08:18.280 --> 08:21.280
He is holding a digital collectibles exhibition on Thursday night.

154
08:21.800 --> 08:23.160
I invited Mr. Deng on his behalf.

155
08:23.240 --> 08:24.640
They will have an in-depth talk then.

156
08:25.520 --> 08:28.600
However, I've been working for Morse lately,

157
08:28.680 --> 08:29.800
so there are things I can't talk about.

158
08:33.080 --> 08:36.000
That's why I'll work on your behalf.

159
08:36.080 --> 08:38.400
You're the irreplaceable, shining

160
08:39.000 --> 08:40.640
Officer Rabbit and girlfriend.

161
08:49.560 --> 08:52.320
‎Mr. Ye, what have you been up to lately? ‎I haven't seen you in a while.

162
08:52.400 --> 08:54.640
‎I've been busy putting together a wedding.

163
08:54.720 --> 08:55.560
‎Oh.

164
09:00.120 --> 09:01.160
-Hello. -Hi.

165
09:01.240 --> 09:02.280
Please come in.

166
09:04.240 --> 09:05.280
Hi.

167
09:06.040 --> 09:06.920
Long time no see.

168
09:07.800 --> 09:10.360
After the event, shall we grab a drink together?

169
09:10.440 --> 09:13.000
No. My partner won't be happy about it.

170
09:15.960 --> 09:17.160
Hi.

171
09:23.680 --> 09:25.000
What did she just say to you?

172
09:26.560 --> 09:27.680
She told me

173
09:27.760 --> 09:29.280
she wanted to ask me out for a drink after the event.

174
09:30.160 --> 09:32.600
I said, "Sorry, I'm afraid my partner would be upset."

175
09:41.600 --> 09:44.160
-Who is your partner? -You.

176
09:45.800 --> 09:47.800
I told you not to buy it.

177
09:47.880 --> 09:49.080
Now we're late, right?

178
09:50.680 --> 09:51.880
They've arrived. I'll greet them.

179
09:52.760 --> 09:54.120
Are you really upset?

180
09:54.200 --> 09:55.760
I said I didn't want to buy it,

181
09:55.840 --> 09:57.840
-but you insisted on buying it now. -What took you two so long?

182
09:57.920 --> 09:59.440
It's all his fault.

183
09:59.520 --> 10:01.400
Right after work, he said we hadn't had dinner

184
10:01.480 --> 10:02.640
and couldn't drink here.

185
10:02.720 --> 10:05.040
Then he parked the car at the convenience store to buy a sandwich.

186
10:05.120 --> 10:06.400
And guess what? We got a ticket.

187
10:09.400 --> 10:11.040
Haven't you known him long enough?

188
10:11.120 --> 10:12.080
He was worried about you.

189
10:13.720 --> 10:16.360
Chi knows me best.

190
10:18.480 --> 10:20.440
Keep an eye on him. Don't let him go off the rails.

191
10:21.560 --> 10:23.080
I have no sway over him.

192
10:27.320 --> 10:28.280
But someone's coming after you.

193
10:48.360 --> 10:49.600
Hello, Mr. Ye.

194
10:51.360 --> 10:53.200
Miss Bu, I've heard so much about you.

195
10:56.800 --> 10:58.280
My turn. Master Ye.

196
11:00.360 --> 11:04.400
I'm Xu Chi's good buddy and Tianna's close friend.

197
11:04.920 --> 11:07.480
I've studied all your classic consulting cases.

198
11:08.920 --> 11:09.960
Just call me Richard.

199
11:10.480 --> 11:11.600
As Chi's boyfriend,

200
11:11.680 --> 11:13.720
I appreciate you looking after her so well at Maxmise.

201
11:14.760 --> 11:16.520
Chi is mine.

202
11:16.600 --> 11:17.760
It's only natural for me to look after her.

203
11:17.840 --> 11:19.000
No need for you to be polite.

204
11:23.880 --> 11:24.680
‎Hey.

205
11:24.760 --> 11:27.040
Excuse me. Du is over there. I have to take my leave.

206
11:29.960 --> 11:31.040
Bye-bye.

207
11:34.560 --> 11:36.480
You just stole his line.

208
11:37.160 --> 11:39.320
Chi already said they've known each other since college.

209
11:39.840 --> 11:41.120
What business was it of mine?

210
11:41.200 --> 11:42.360
He comes after me.

211
11:43.000 --> 11:44.120
Help me touch up my makeup.

212
11:49.480 --> 11:51.360
What's going on between you two?

213
11:51.960 --> 11:54.080
Why did you suddenly ask me to this exhibition?

214
11:54.160 --> 11:56.240
You were so mysterious on the phone.

215
11:56.760 --> 11:57.920
And your outfit…

216
11:58.000 --> 11:59.440
What's wrong with my outfit?

217
12:00.080 --> 12:02.040
You don't look like you are under investigation

218
12:02.120 --> 12:03.240
for suspected financial issues.

219
12:03.320 --> 12:04.960
You look like you're here to take photos.

220
12:05.040 --> 12:07.120
Actually, you'd look great in photos wearing this.

221
12:07.200 --> 12:08.960
Then take one for me. Here.

222
12:09.720 --> 12:10.920
Come on.

223
12:11.000 --> 12:12.480
What's going on? Spill it.

224
12:14.240 --> 12:15.800
He has a side project,

225
12:15.880 --> 12:17.680
but he can't show up in person.

226
12:17.760 --> 12:19.560
Since I'm free now, I'm just helping him out.

227
12:19.640 --> 12:21.040
Are you two really together?

228
12:28.640 --> 12:31.920
But is there no risk of you working on that side project for him?

229
12:32.800 --> 12:33.960
He strung you along before,

230
12:34.640 --> 12:36.240
but now he's preying on you.

231
12:36.320 --> 12:37.160
This is a romance scam.

232
12:38.680 --> 12:40.600
I know you're worried about me, but trust me.

233
12:40.680 --> 12:42.320
I can judge this for myself, okay?

234
12:44.720 --> 12:47.080
How much judgment can a woman in love possibly have?

235
12:47.160 --> 12:48.480
I know that too well.

236
12:53.640 --> 12:56.040
He brought me here today, and without the slightest hesitation,

237
12:56.120 --> 12:57.400
announced to everyone that I'm his girlfriend.

238
12:57.480 --> 13:00.040
Meanwhile, they're still investigating me.

239
13:00.120 --> 13:01.320
Do you know what this means?

240
13:03.880 --> 13:06.960
It means he's staking his own reputation in the consulting circle to vouch for me.

241
13:08.120 --> 13:10.000
That alone is tremendous support for me.

242
13:10.080 --> 13:11.600
Your matter will surely be fine.

243
13:13.600 --> 13:16.760
Now you should enjoy yourself while you're on leave.

244
13:17.280 --> 13:18.800
Once you get through this ordeal,

245
13:18.880 --> 13:20.920
you'll be back at Maxmise working hard.

246
13:21.000 --> 13:22.440
He's always off on business trips,

247
13:22.520 --> 13:24.400
and you'll be pulling all-nighters at work.

248
13:24.480 --> 13:26.640
Even if you manage to set up a date, you'll have to cross-check your schedules.

249
13:26.720 --> 13:27.640
Let me tell you,

250
13:27.720 --> 13:30.600
even over a candlelit dinner, you'll get four or five work calls.

251
13:30.680 --> 13:31.800
It'll be absolutely miserable.

252
13:34.440 --> 13:35.280
Absolutely miserable?

253
13:36.240 --> 13:39.160
So you've imagined this scene many times in your head?

254
13:41.840 --> 13:42.880
With who?

255
13:47.880 --> 13:49.200
Alright.

256
13:49.280 --> 13:52.040
You said you wanted to broaden your network beyond your dad.

257
13:53.000 --> 13:53.920
I'll introduce you to a few people today.

258
13:56.640 --> 13:57.600
Let's go.

259
13:57.680 --> 13:58.880
Take it slow.

260
14:03.160 --> 14:05.600
He actually knows people here?

261
14:08.280 --> 14:09.920
He doesn't seem to be happy.

262
14:10.000 --> 14:11.320
Although now Zhao Heng

263
14:11.400 --> 14:13.440
flies all over the place and stays at high-end hotels,

264
14:13.520 --> 14:15.600
he was remarkably frugal when he was a student.

265
14:16.880 --> 14:18.840
-I think it was during undergrad, right? -Yes.

266
14:18.920 --> 14:20.120
We went to the US for a summer camp together.

267
14:20.920 --> 14:22.360
He and I took direct flights,

268
14:22.440 --> 14:24.440
but this guy transferred for over 40 hours

269
14:24.520 --> 14:25.760
just to save a few hundred US dollars.

270
14:25.840 --> 14:27.000
-Right? -Yeah.

271
14:27.080 --> 14:28.320
-I'm not mistaken, am I? -Back in school,

272
14:28.400 --> 14:29.680
I wanted to save some money.

273
14:30.280 --> 14:31.440
This guy was not only thrifty,

274
14:31.520 --> 14:33.040
but also great at making ends meet.

275
14:33.560 --> 14:35.120
-Back then, we stayed in… -A homestay.

276
14:35.200 --> 14:36.120
Yeah, a homestay.

277
14:36.200 --> 14:37.840
The meal plan was included, 70 US dollars a month.

278
14:37.920 --> 14:38.840
-We all signed up for it. -Yeah.

279
14:38.920 --> 14:39.760
Only he didn't.

280
14:39.840 --> 14:43.400
He took the bus to discount supermarkets and bought these huge bags of bread.

281
14:43.480 --> 14:44.800
Without even any jam.

282
14:45.840 --> 14:47.080
Back then, I made a bet with him.

283
14:47.160 --> 14:49.360
I said, as the summer camp lasts two months,

284
14:49.440 --> 14:51.040
he couldn't stick to plain food every day.

285
14:51.120 --> 14:52.680
And guess what happened?

286
14:52.760 --> 14:54.720
-Mexican restaurant, right? -Mexican restaurant, yeah.

287
14:54.800 --> 14:56.280
He collected leftover duck necks

288
14:56.360 --> 14:59.160
and chicken feet from there and braised them in a pot.

289
15:00.080 --> 15:01.440
It smelled amazing that day!

290
15:01.520 --> 15:03.120
I still remember that taste.

291
15:03.200 --> 15:04.640
No wonder when I saw you from afar just now…

292
15:04.720 --> 15:05.960
-Keep your poser company, -I didn't recognize you just now.

293
15:06.040 --> 15:07.040
-and I'll go and check. -Couldn't even place your name.

294
15:07.120 --> 15:08.840
Two duck necks instantly popped into my head.

295
15:10.240 --> 15:11.640
When will you braise for us again?

296
15:11.720 --> 15:12.560
Sure, I'll make it for you.

297
15:12.640 --> 15:13.960
Alright, how about

298
15:14.040 --> 15:15.840
I change my WeChat avatar to two duck necks later?

299
15:15.920 --> 15:17.680
-Okay, it's a promise. -Don't you dare.

300
15:19.120 --> 15:21.480
Your WeChat avatar has to be a photo I pick.

301
15:38.200 --> 15:39.760
Who even are they?

302
15:39.840 --> 15:42.240
They don't even know me, yet they dare come to a place like this.

303
15:43.080 --> 15:44.240
They're my college classmates.

304
15:45.120 --> 15:46.240
We were roommates.

305
15:46.320 --> 15:47.560
College classmates?

306
15:48.960 --> 15:51.280
Your college roommates still don't know you braised duck necks in the US

307
15:51.360 --> 15:53.040
because I love them?

308
15:54.360 --> 15:55.880
Honey, stay away from them.

309
15:55.960 --> 15:57.440
You're being so childish.

310
15:57.520 --> 15:59.160
For us women,

311
15:59.240 --> 16:00.680
when people take our kindness for weakness,

312
16:00.760 --> 16:02.120
acting all chummy to our faces

313
16:02.200 --> 16:04.400
yet dripping with subtle sarcasm and making sly digs at me,

314
16:04.480 --> 16:06.120
I'd have exposed them all over WeChat Moments long before.

315
16:06.200 --> 16:07.240
I…

316
16:09.000 --> 16:10.920
Alright, less arguing.

317
16:12.800 --> 16:16.600
Tianna and I are going over there to greet some friends. You folks chat.

318
16:16.680 --> 16:18.720
-It's fine. Go ahead. -Go on.

319
16:19.360 --> 16:20.200
Let's go.

320
16:23.160 --> 16:23.960
You're in my way.

321
16:29.640 --> 16:30.840
Be right back.

322
16:32.040 --> 16:33.120
She's got what it takes.

323
16:33.200 --> 16:36.040
That bag is a limited edition.

324
16:36.120 --> 16:38.240
-I saw through it at once. -No wonder.

325
16:38.880 --> 16:39.760
Come here.

326
16:40.680 --> 16:41.720
Fix my hair.

327
16:42.720 --> 16:44.440
Fix my hair! Hurry. They're watching.

328
16:51.040 --> 16:51.720
Aren't you such a charmer?

329
16:51.800 --> 16:53.160
Bring out all those tricks you used to pursue me.

330
16:56.240 --> 16:57.440
Come closer to me.

331
16:57.520 --> 17:00.040
How come you're stunned after hearing what they said?

332
17:26.800 --> 17:29.720
Your earring is crooked.

333
17:31.760 --> 17:33.200
What are you thinking?

334
17:44.520 --> 17:45.480
Gentle.

335
17:46.000 --> 17:47.320
They are still watching.

336
17:54.680 --> 17:55.520
Thank you.

337
17:57.320 --> 17:59.600
I used to fight alone out there.

338
18:01.240 --> 18:02.880
This is my first time being protected.

339
18:04.040 --> 18:05.120
It feels sweet.

340
18:08.000 --> 18:09.080
So nice.

341
18:17.920 --> 18:19.600
Fighting alone?

342
18:20.200 --> 18:23.680
I wonder what lousy places you used to go to.

343
18:23.760 --> 18:25.600
That's why you got intimidated the second you came here.

344
18:26.400 --> 18:28.400
Obviously, you get bullied by them, yet you were grinning foolishly.

345
18:29.080 --> 18:31.200
It's okay. With you protecting me, I fear nothing.

346
18:33.320 --> 18:35.480
Why would I protect you? What exactly are we to each other?

347
18:35.560 --> 18:37.640
We're just colleagues.

348
18:38.240 --> 18:39.920
You're colleagues with Chi too, and you protect her as well.

349
18:40.640 --> 18:42.240
Well, I… I…

350
18:42.320 --> 18:43.680
Speak of the devil.

351
18:44.880 --> 18:46.000
She's waving at us.

352
18:47.480 --> 18:48.760
Let's go.

353
18:52.200 --> 18:53.120
Mind your manners.

354
18:55.320 --> 18:56.800
Didn't you teach me that?

355
18:56.880 --> 18:58.040
Let's go.

356
19:00.280 --> 19:02.360
-That's wonderful. -Yeah.

357
19:02.440 --> 19:03.520
-I saw this last time. -You saw it last time.

358
19:03.600 --> 19:04.880
-We've talked about it. -Right.

359
19:04.960 --> 19:05.800
Hello.

360
19:05.880 --> 19:07.360
-Let's shake hands. Come on. -Hello, Mr. Deng.

361
19:07.440 --> 19:08.680
Hello. You look stunning.

362
19:08.760 --> 19:10.440
Hope you'll get the chance to work together in the future.

363
19:10.520 --> 19:11.760
Sure.

364
19:11.840 --> 19:14.280
This lady looks very familiar to me.

365
19:16.000 --> 19:17.040
-Long time no see. -Long time no see.

366
19:17.120 --> 19:18.040
Hello.

367
19:18.120 --> 19:19.880
-Any new work recently? -This is your…

368
19:19.960 --> 19:21.000
My father.

369
19:21.080 --> 19:23.280
Which firm does he…

370
19:23.360 --> 19:25.240
Excuse me. I need to step away.

371
19:25.320 --> 19:26.160
Carry on.

372
19:30.720 --> 19:32.840
-Nervous? -A little.

373
19:34.200 --> 19:35.280
Take a deep breath.

374
19:35.920 --> 19:37.120
Let's go over our plan again.

375
19:40.360 --> 19:41.560
You work behind the scenes, I take the stage.

376
19:41.640 --> 19:42.560
We'll act as intermediaries,

377
19:42.640 --> 19:44.480
brokering financing between Wen Ruosen and Morse.

378
19:44.560 --> 19:48.160
But we'll advise Morse to set extremely demanding wager terms.

379
19:48.240 --> 19:51.560
If Wen Ruosen wants the investment, he has to stake everything he owns.

380
19:51.640 --> 19:53.080
Because your analysis shows

381
19:53.160 --> 19:55.120
that risks in the digital collectibles market have built up to a high level.

382
19:55.200 --> 19:56.560
Once in a recession,

383
19:56.640 --> 19:58.200
market values will plummet across the board.

384
19:58.280 --> 20:01.080
By then, Wen Ruosen will definitely lose this wager.

385
20:03.240 --> 20:04.480
One question.

386
20:05.520 --> 20:07.040
What if we introduce them to each other,

387
20:07.120 --> 20:08.720
and they cut us out to negotiate directly?

388
20:10.240 --> 20:11.240
That won't happen.

389
20:11.800 --> 20:12.880
Then they'd break the rules.

390
20:13.640 --> 20:14.520
Besides,

391
20:14.600 --> 20:17.120
they haven't known each other long enough to trust each other.

392
20:18.560 --> 20:20.320
Wen Ruosen desperately needs capital.

393
20:20.400 --> 20:23.840
If he wants to push the financing process forward efficiently and quickly,

394
20:23.920 --> 20:25.960
he has to use a third party like us.

395
20:26.040 --> 20:29.000
Simply put, this is a small-scale financing consultation.

396
20:29.600 --> 20:31.440
Okay. One more thing.

397
20:32.400 --> 20:35.040
If Yuanzhou Gallery really blows up,

398
20:35.640 --> 20:36.920
will we end up hurting Morse and Mr. Deng?

399
20:38.560 --> 20:40.040
Absolutely not.

400
20:40.640 --> 20:42.400
We're facilitating a transaction,

401
20:42.480 --> 20:43.800
not fabricating anything.

402
20:44.920 --> 20:47.480
As one of the world's most experienced investment banks,

403
20:47.560 --> 20:49.200
Morse has their own professional evaluation models.

404
20:49.800 --> 20:51.840
So even if our plan works, nothing bad will happen to Deng.

405
20:53.160 --> 20:54.000
Sure,

406
20:54.080 --> 20:56.440
I hope Wen Ruosen reaps what he sows soon.

407
20:56.520 --> 20:59.840
But I'm not some bloodthirsty monster who will stop at nothing just for revenge.

408
21:03.800 --> 21:05.040
I can be the monster too.

409
21:05.720 --> 21:07.520
You're the beauty, and I'm the beast.

410
21:09.760 --> 21:11.320
Can't you stop joking at a time like this?

411
21:12.720 --> 21:13.920
You're not nervous anymore.

412
21:17.360 --> 21:18.560
Now,

413
21:19.160 --> 21:20.240
it's your time to shine.

414
21:25.400 --> 21:26.240
-Hello. -Xinzhi.

415
21:26.320 --> 21:27.000
-Sir. -Miss Xu.

416
21:27.080 --> 21:28.200
-Mr. Wen. -This is Mr. Deng.

417
21:28.720 --> 21:29.720
-Hello, Mr. Deng. -Hello.

418
21:39.480 --> 21:41.280
Alright, I've got the general picture.

419
21:41.360 --> 21:44.240
Since Richard recommended this, I'll make sure to arrange it properly.

420
21:45.360 --> 21:47.600
It wasn't Richard, but Miss Xu.

421
21:48.960 --> 21:49.840
My memory's failing me.

422
21:49.920 --> 21:53.000
I forgot Richard is busy with the project between Tianhe Air and us.

423
21:53.640 --> 21:54.960
He can't get involved in other projects.

424
21:55.560 --> 21:58.320
Miss Xu is the matchmaker for this project.

425
21:58.400 --> 21:59.240
Yes, that's right.

426
21:59.840 --> 22:00.880
She's been on leave recently.

427
22:00.960 --> 22:02.280
I'm glad you don't mind her limited experience

428
22:02.360 --> 22:03.520
and are willing to mentor her.

429
22:03.600 --> 22:04.920
I won't stand on ceremony.

430
22:05.440 --> 22:06.680
No need to stand on ceremony.

431
22:06.760 --> 22:08.000
Let's celebrate.

432
22:08.080 --> 22:09.920
-Cheers. -Cheers.

433
22:10.440 --> 22:12.320
-Happy cooperation. -Happy cooperation.

434
22:16.720 --> 22:17.920
I'm worn out.

435
22:48.760 --> 22:49.600
I can do it myself.

436
22:50.400 --> 22:51.640
Take the other one off too.

437
22:52.640 --> 22:54.600
Just relax. You've had a tough day.

438
23:17.240 --> 23:18.320
I'm fine.

439
23:19.040 --> 23:19.880
I've got you here.

440
23:28.240 --> 23:29.320
What are you laughing at?

441
23:31.640 --> 23:34.200
I just had a really childish thought.

442
23:35.040 --> 23:37.240
I wish time could freeze right at this moment.

443
23:41.440 --> 23:44.960
Sure. I'll cast my magic. Give me your hand.

444
23:49.760 --> 23:51.240
Close your eyes.

445
23:52.080 --> 23:53.760
Let's feel it together.

446
24:54.000 --> 24:56.600
Alright, it's done. The magic ends.

447
24:57.200 --> 24:58.120
Already?

448
24:59.640 --> 25:00.720
Barely a moment.

449
25:02.360 --> 25:03.400
It's enough.

450
25:04.240 --> 25:07.880
You've already given me more than enough.

451
25:10.640 --> 25:12.520
Actually, during the reception today,

452
25:13.120 --> 25:14.840
I felt everything was so surreal.

453
25:17.960 --> 25:18.920
Thank you.

454
25:19.000 --> 25:21.760
Back there, in front of Tianna, you saved me plenty of face.

455
25:21.840 --> 25:25.920
You introduced her to so many people and looked out for Zhao Heng.

456
25:28.040 --> 25:31.160
Tianna didn't say anything out loud, but she's grateful deep down.

457
25:31.760 --> 25:32.760
She is from the Bu family.

458
25:32.840 --> 25:35.640
Isn't she totally at home at events like this?

459
25:35.720 --> 25:37.160
Why would she need my introduction?

460
25:37.240 --> 25:38.240
That's not the case.

461
25:38.880 --> 25:41.320
Today she wasn't there as the eldest daughter of the Bu family,

462
25:41.400 --> 25:44.320
but as Bu Tianna.

463
25:49.600 --> 25:50.800
You're what matters most.

464
25:52.560 --> 25:53.400
How did you find today?

465
25:56.320 --> 25:59.720
I think today was amazing.

466
26:00.440 --> 26:01.400
I mean it.

467
26:01.920 --> 26:06.800
It feels like I'm holding a thread in my hand,

468
26:06.880 --> 26:10.440
and I'm carefully gathering pearls of all different shapes.

469
26:10.520 --> 26:15.160
Someday I'll turn them into a dazzling necklace.

470
26:15.760 --> 26:16.640
Really.

471
26:16.720 --> 26:19.200
I think if our goal this time weren't to take Wen…

472
26:30.000 --> 26:31.280
The weather is nice outside.

473
26:31.360 --> 26:32.560
How about going for a walk out there?

474
26:32.640 --> 26:34.280
My feet don't hurt anyway.

475
26:34.840 --> 26:35.920
Alright.

476
26:37.840 --> 26:39.800
Don't be mad.

477
26:40.320 --> 26:42.320
I was thinking

478
26:42.400 --> 26:44.920
that if our goal this time weren't to take Wen Ruosen down,

479
26:45.000 --> 26:46.000
but to truly expand and strengthen

480
26:46.080 --> 26:48.040
Yuanzhou Digital Collectibles through financing,

481
26:48.120 --> 26:49.760
it'd have been quite interesting.

482
26:51.520 --> 26:55.360
Sometimes I was also thinking that if Wen Ruosen got lucky,

483
26:55.440 --> 26:57.560
or the regulatory policies hadn't come out so soon,

484
26:58.200 --> 26:59.800
I would have helped him.

485
27:00.480 --> 27:01.840
But there's no way around it.

486
27:01.920 --> 27:03.920
Since I chose an open scheme,

487
27:04.000 --> 27:05.560
I can't change the strategy.

488
27:06.440 --> 27:08.680
If you like financing consultation work,

489
27:09.200 --> 27:11.600
I can take you on more deals later.

490
27:12.120 --> 27:13.240
Great.

491
27:14.880 --> 27:17.680
If we close this deal for them,

492
27:17.760 --> 27:21.080
will we get this according to industry rules?

493
27:21.800 --> 27:24.360
For a favor deal like this,

494
27:24.440 --> 27:26.080
if it were to succeed,

495
27:26.640 --> 27:28.000
no less than 1%.

496
27:28.560 --> 27:30.400
That would cover the down payment for your mother's apartment.

497
27:32.240 --> 27:33.360
I remember everything you've said.

498
27:35.880 --> 27:36.880
But watch my wording.

499
27:36.960 --> 27:38.440
If it were to succeed.

500
27:38.520 --> 27:39.760
The subjunctive mood.

501
27:40.320 --> 27:42.520
So, we both need to work hard.

502
27:51.560 --> 27:53.280
I will do my best

503
27:53.360 --> 27:57.120
because this is my first chance to follow you

504
27:57.200 --> 27:59.920
and do a full project from start to finish.

505
28:00.440 --> 28:03.480
I have to prove that I'm qualified and capable

506
28:03.560 --> 28:04.840
of standing behind you and working with you.

507
28:06.080 --> 28:08.320
Not behind, but beside.

508
28:25.920 --> 28:28.000
Last time I made the first move.

509
28:28.080 --> 28:30.720
This time it's up to you.

510
28:49.120 --> 28:51.320
I wish time could freeze right at this moment.

511
28:51.400 --> 28:52.640
Give me your hand.

512
28:52.720 --> 28:54.120
Close your eyes.

513
28:54.720 --> 28:56.400
Let's feel it together.

514
29:06.400 --> 29:07.760
He means it.

515
29:24.800 --> 29:26.000
Still nothing.

516
29:28.720 --> 29:30.120
Then I'm leaving.

517
29:30.200 --> 29:31.720
I'm heading back.

518
30:08.480 --> 30:11.320
What consultant rests this early?

519
30:11.880 --> 30:13.000
That's so unprofessional.

520
30:13.760 --> 30:16.960
I want to talk to you about the plan for Wen Ruosen.

521
30:25.480 --> 30:26.640
Sure.

522
30:27.280 --> 30:29.960
Then, Richard,

523
30:30.040 --> 30:32.320
may I come over to your place to work overtime on the plan?

524
30:33.400 --> 30:34.640
Of course you can.

525
30:35.160 --> 30:36.800
I've got some fine red wine at home.

526
30:36.880 --> 30:38.480
We can work while drinking red wine.

527
30:40.720 --> 30:41.720
Work while drinking?

528
30:45.640 --> 30:46.640
No.

529
30:47.200 --> 30:48.640
I… I was joking.

530
30:48.720 --> 30:51.600
You see, no one's at my place during the day.

531
30:51.680 --> 30:54.120
There's a printer, and the sofa is comfy.

532
30:54.200 --> 30:57.400
I hope you can work comfortably when working for me.

533
31:05.920 --> 31:07.000
Is that okay?

534
32:12.640 --> 32:14.760
I can't accept this reason.

535
32:14.840 --> 32:17.400
Vincent, if you think I'm easy to push around,

536
32:17.480 --> 32:18.960
then it'll end here.

537
32:22.040 --> 32:23.160
You're back.

538
32:23.880 --> 32:24.880
Let's leave it at that.

539
32:24.960 --> 32:25.800
We'll be in touch.

540
32:28.880 --> 32:31.200
Sorry. I made such a mess here.

541
32:31.280 --> 32:32.200
It's fine.

542
32:32.720 --> 32:33.880
But what happened to you?

543
32:33.960 --> 32:35.680
Why did you suddenly blow up at Wen Ruosen?

544
32:36.640 --> 32:39.720
He thinks the proposal we offered is far too harsh.

545
32:39.800 --> 32:40.880
He even changed

546
32:40.960 --> 32:42.920
just two figures in the documents we prepared

547
32:43.000 --> 32:44.760
and went to other small investment funds,

548
32:44.840 --> 32:46.080
trying to get them to agree.

549
32:46.160 --> 32:48.520
Then he'd use that to pressure Morse and us.

550
32:50.480 --> 32:51.400
Why get so upset over this?

551
32:51.480 --> 32:54.160
Didn't we expect this before?

552
32:54.760 --> 32:55.800
I know.

553
32:55.880 --> 32:57.240
Du passed this news to me.

554
32:58.400 --> 33:00.160
You said Wen Ruosen would

555
33:00.840 --> 33:03.000
hit a wall and come back,

556
33:03.080 --> 33:05.120
so I poured oil on that fire, and I lost my temper with him on purpose.

557
33:06.360 --> 33:07.200
I threw the documents

558
33:07.280 --> 33:09.280
to make the background drama sound convincing.

559
33:10.080 --> 33:11.760
As a steady, seasoned partner,

560
33:11.840 --> 33:13.440
you definitely wouldn't abandon the whole matchmaking deal

561
33:13.520 --> 33:15.080
just because of minor setbacks.

562
33:15.160 --> 33:16.480
But I'm different.

563
33:16.560 --> 33:18.280
I'm an impulsive young girl.

564
33:18.360 --> 33:20.440
If I fly off the handle and pull out,

565
33:20.520 --> 33:22.640
he won't get funding from either side and will be more anxious.

566
33:24.000 --> 33:24.920
It was an act.

567
33:26.000 --> 33:26.880
You really took a big risk.

568
33:28.040 --> 33:29.560
Don't worry.

569
33:29.640 --> 33:31.480
I know exactly what I'm doing.

570
33:32.000 --> 33:33.560
I checked his natal chart.

571
33:33.640 --> 33:34.960
He's a Libra,

572
33:35.040 --> 33:36.480
with the Moon in Capricorn.

573
33:36.560 --> 33:38.800
So when big issues come up, he's bound to hesitate.

574
33:39.640 --> 33:41.640
Suspicious, yet craving control.

575
33:41.720 --> 33:43.520
I even looked up his MBTI. He…

576
33:43.600 --> 33:45.320
You rely on horoscopes for matters like this?

577
33:46.880 --> 33:51.400
But I think PDP behavioral testing is much the same as horoscopes.

578
33:53.600 --> 33:55.720
Fine, let me put it another way.

579
33:55.800 --> 33:57.400
He has a chameleon personality.

580
33:57.480 --> 33:58.720
He blows with the wind.

581
33:58.800 --> 34:00.440
He seems bold on the surface,

582
34:00.520 --> 34:01.720
but deep down, he's really timid.

583
34:01.800 --> 34:03.480
That's why I'm pulling a hard move. It might work wonders.

584
34:04.160 --> 34:07.600
I just greeted you on purpose to let him hear us.

585
34:07.680 --> 34:10.800
I guess he must be in a real fluster right now.

586
34:10.880 --> 34:12.880
He'll probably call you shortly to sound you out.

587
34:24.920 --> 34:26.239
WEN RUOSEN

588
34:26.320 --> 34:28.440
See? I was right.

589
34:29.199 --> 34:31.800
Hang up on him. Two minutes later, call him back,

590
34:31.880 --> 34:33.840
tell him you were calming me down, and reproach him a little.

591
34:35.320 --> 34:36.400
Hang up.

592
34:38.080 --> 34:40.480
Just do as I say this time. Please.

593
34:45.440 --> 34:46.520
Thank you.

594
34:49.320 --> 34:51.000
She was overly emotional just now.

595
34:51.080 --> 34:52.360
I really couldn't take the call.

596
34:52.960 --> 34:54.040
It's my fault.

597
34:54.120 --> 34:56.400
I didn't expect her to have such a fierce temper.

598
34:56.480 --> 34:57.680
I've embarrassed you.

599
35:01.920 --> 35:04.240
Mr. Wen, about this matter,

600
35:04.320 --> 35:05.320
let me say something.

601
35:05.400 --> 35:07.480
You moved a bit too hastily on this.

602
35:08.280 --> 35:11.000
Financing has lead and follow-on investment roles.

603
35:12.200 --> 35:14.000
We'd nearly got everything lined up for you.

604
35:14.600 --> 35:17.760
Why did you bypass us and go through all this trouble?

605
35:18.800 --> 35:19.720
It wasn't like that.

606
35:20.240 --> 35:22.560
They thought Morse was going to invest in me,

607
35:22.640 --> 35:24.760
so they pestered me with all kinds of questions.

608
35:25.720 --> 35:27.320
That's what made Miss Xu misunderstand.

609
35:29.240 --> 35:32.360
Yes. I just said a couple of words on your behalf,

610
35:32.440 --> 35:33.880
and she sent me out onto the terrace.

611
35:34.840 --> 35:36.760
As I told you before,

612
35:37.960 --> 35:40.760
she had a tough time at Maxmise.

613
35:41.360 --> 35:45.080
So I brought her here to let her unwind

614
35:45.160 --> 35:48.360
and to see if Chi and I can help you.

615
35:48.440 --> 35:50.640
It's my way to repay your support back then.

616
35:51.800 --> 35:53.280
But as things stand,

617
35:55.520 --> 35:58.640
maybe Chi and I should withdraw from this project.

618
35:58.720 --> 36:01.440
No. You mustn't do that.

619
36:01.520 --> 36:02.400
It's a minor misunderstanding.

620
36:03.440 --> 36:04.360
Yes.

621
36:13.920 --> 36:15.000
Well?

622
36:16.120 --> 36:18.320
This truly is my bottom line.

623
36:20.000 --> 36:21.240
Alright, I understand.

624
36:21.320 --> 36:24.720
Well, I'll try to persuade Chi later.

625
36:25.240 --> 36:26.680
If it falls through,

626
36:26.760 --> 36:28.880
I'll do my best to negotiate with Deng on your behalf.

627
36:28.960 --> 36:30.000
Okay?

628
36:32.040 --> 36:33.040
Okay, thank you.

629
37:17.680 --> 37:19.600
Your appointment letter. I nearly forgot it.

630
37:22.240 --> 37:23.880
I was planning to fetch it myself.

631
37:23.960 --> 37:25.480
Didn't expect you'd bring it over.

632
37:25.560 --> 37:26.680
By the way,

633
37:26.760 --> 37:28.600
the Academic Affairs Office assigned me a course.

634
37:29.120 --> 37:31.160
Strategic Analysis. The first class is next Saturday.

635
37:31.760 --> 37:33.280
Great, that's wonderful.

636
37:33.360 --> 37:34.760
Everything will fall into place.

637
37:35.640 --> 37:38.240
Now all matters are proceeding as planned.

638
37:39.200 --> 37:40.400
How about Wen Ruosen?

639
37:41.600 --> 37:42.640
He took the bait.

640
37:43.160 --> 37:45.800
So we're three months ahead of our original plan?

641
37:45.880 --> 37:46.640
Yes.

642
37:47.280 --> 37:49.120
He basically accepted the terms I drafted for Morse.

643
37:49.200 --> 37:52.160
Morse will subscribe to 38% equity of Wen Ruosen's Yuanzhou.

644
37:52.240 --> 37:54.080
Yuanzhou promises a minimum 25% compound annual growth rate

645
37:54.160 --> 37:55.240
in performance.

646
37:55.840 --> 37:57.520
Failing that, Wen Ruosen shall repurchase all shares

647
37:57.600 --> 37:59.480
at a compound annual interest rate of 13%.

648
38:01.240 --> 38:03.200
Twenty-five percent won't work at all.

649
38:03.280 --> 38:04.840
Initially, we set it at 40%.

650
38:05.440 --> 38:07.040
The digital collectible market is red-hot right now.

651
38:07.120 --> 38:09.720
What if he tries hard and actually hits over 25%?

652
38:09.800 --> 38:11.520
Then we'd end up helping him.

653
38:12.720 --> 38:13.880
This is all he promised.

654
38:13.960 --> 38:15.560
But Chi added one clause to the agreement

655
38:15.640 --> 38:18.600
that Morse accepts market value fluctuations within normal ranges.

656
38:18.680 --> 38:22.400
Yet the lower bound for the normal range in the addendum is set at minus 30%.

657
38:22.480 --> 38:26.280
Namely, if Yuanzhou Digital Collectibles drops to 70% of its market value,

658
38:26.360 --> 38:28.320
the company's full ownership will transfer to Morse.

659
38:30.920 --> 38:33.200
That girl really delivered.

660
38:33.280 --> 38:35.000
Has nobody from their team found out about this?

661
38:35.080 --> 38:36.280
They haven't.

662
38:36.360 --> 38:38.040
They were totally wrapped up

663
38:38.120 --> 38:39.880
in arguing whether the performance commitment

664
38:39.960 --> 38:41.480
should be 25% or 40%.

665
38:41.560 --> 38:42.880
When I went to pick up Chi,

666
38:42.960 --> 38:44.440
I noticed Wen Ruosen's back was soaked.

667
38:45.040 --> 38:46.840
His legal team was chugging Red Bull nonstop.

668
38:47.440 --> 38:48.280
With this tactic,

669
38:48.360 --> 38:49.760
she wore them down completely,

670
38:49.840 --> 38:51.000
leaving them no bandwidth to check anything else.

671
38:56.160 --> 38:58.200
I wouldn't call him authoritative,

672
38:58.280 --> 39:00.480
but everyone does reference his data.

673
39:00.560 --> 39:01.480
Yeah.

674
39:06.640 --> 39:07.480
What…

675
39:08.000 --> 39:10.320
What's this?

676
39:11.720 --> 39:13.600
Have you two already…

677
39:15.440 --> 39:16.800
We had.

678
39:18.400 --> 39:22.280
You old dog, nice work.

679
39:22.800 --> 39:25.240
At the reception that night, I thought you were putting on an act.

680
39:25.320 --> 39:26.440
Come on.

681
39:26.520 --> 39:29.080
Every time you see me, all we talk about is work.

682
39:29.160 --> 39:30.880
Why didn't you update me on such big news?

683
39:30.960 --> 39:32.080
How far have you gotten?

684
39:32.600 --> 39:33.880
Actually, not that far.

685
39:34.800 --> 39:37.920
The moment I saw her with another man,

686
39:38.000 --> 39:39.320
I knew I was done for.

687
39:40.360 --> 39:43.960
Your tone doesn't sound right.

688
39:44.040 --> 39:46.320
With your capability, you fear you can't control her?

689
39:47.680 --> 39:51.000
Not exactly. But she's changed me a lot.

690
39:51.920 --> 39:55.520
So are you worried she's too sharp,

691
39:55.600 --> 39:56.840
or…

692
40:01.320 --> 40:04.160
For instance, I thought I'd observed Wen Ruosen long enough

693
40:04.240 --> 40:05.640
to know him inside out.

694
40:05.720 --> 40:10.480
So I kept spinning the net step by step, hoping to slowly trap him.

695
40:11.320 --> 40:12.200
‎-Xinzhi. ‎-Sir.

696
40:12.280 --> 40:13.960
-Miss Xu. -This is Mr. Deng.

697
40:14.040 --> 40:15.760
-Hi, Mr. Deng. -I checked his natal chart.

698
40:15.840 --> 40:17.200
He's a Libra.

699
40:17.280 --> 40:18.320
Yet I never imagined

700
40:19.040 --> 40:21.040
Chi would use horoscopes and MBTI,

701
40:21.120 --> 40:24.000
things I used to dismiss, to analyze his character.

702
40:24.080 --> 40:25.680
And she actually got him right.

703
40:25.760 --> 40:26.840
You rely on horoscopes?

704
40:26.920 --> 40:28.720
If you think I'm easy to push around,

705
40:28.800 --> 40:30.240
then it'll end here.

706
40:31.760 --> 40:34.080
Later, without letting me know,

707
40:34.160 --> 40:36.000
she blew up on purpose

708
40:36.080 --> 40:38.240
and broke through Wen Ruosen's psychological defenses.

709
40:38.320 --> 40:40.880
You said Wen Ruosen would

710
40:40.960 --> 40:43.920
hit a wall and come back eventually, so I poured oil on that fire,

711
40:44.000 --> 40:45.360
and I lost my temper with him on purpose.

712
40:45.440 --> 40:46.720
Well?

713
40:46.800 --> 40:48.720
This truly is my bottom line.

714
40:50.120 --> 40:51.360
Alright, I understand.

715
40:51.440 --> 40:52.920
Okay, thank you.

716
40:53.000 --> 40:57.040
The second Wen Ruosen agreed to accept Chi's terms,

717
40:57.120 --> 41:00.600
I even asked myself whether I'd fallen behind

718
41:00.680 --> 41:03.720
and lost the sharp insight I once prided myself on.

719
41:05.760 --> 41:07.640
Of course I'm not scared of her growing more capable.

720
41:08.320 --> 41:11.760
I truly hope she can fly higher and higher.

721
41:11.840 --> 41:13.280
After all, she's immensely talented.

722
41:14.360 --> 41:15.560
Lots of her moves and ideas

723
41:15.640 --> 41:17.240
surpass what I can comprehend.

724
41:18.520 --> 41:20.840
She fills me with a deep respect for the younger generation.

725
41:23.760 --> 41:25.720
You've had it far too easy over these years.

726
41:25.800 --> 41:26.840
Everything went smoothly for you.

727
41:26.920 --> 41:28.760
You've never faced any setbacks. Right?

728
41:28.840 --> 41:29.720
Now you're facing setbacks.

729
41:29.800 --> 41:31.360
Whether you like to hear it or not, I'm going to say it.

730
41:31.440 --> 41:32.520
You're…

731
41:32.600 --> 41:34.560
You're just too solitary.

732
41:34.640 --> 41:36.240
You struggle to trust others.

733
41:36.760 --> 41:38.360
It took us four or five years working together

734
41:38.440 --> 41:40.280
before we opened up to each other.

735
41:40.360 --> 41:43.040
Now you've met a girl whom you can't get control.

736
41:43.120 --> 41:45.200
No wonder you're lost.

737
41:46.360 --> 41:48.520
Deep down, you think she liked you at first

738
41:48.600 --> 41:50.400
because she looked up to you.

739
41:50.480 --> 41:52.080
But now that you're dating, growing close

740
41:52.160 --> 41:54.240
and seeing each other plainly,

741
41:54.320 --> 41:55.520
the mystery fades,

742
41:55.600 --> 41:58.400
and your untouchable aura is gone, right?
